WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:07.000
Building a Schedule of Loss means pulling facts from contracts, payslips and letters, then checking the figures.

00:00:07.000 --> 00:00:13.000
With Lylo, drop in the case documents and the draft starts building from the evidence.

00:00:13.000 --> 00:00:21.500
Key details, the basic award, past and future losses, and pension loss are brought together in one structured draft.

00:00:21.500 --> 00:00:27.000
Open Citations to see the exact document and page behind each figure.

00:00:27.000 --> 00:00:33.000
Calculations shows the working behind each total, so the maths can be checked.

00:00:33.000 --> 00:00:46.000
When the documents cannot establish something, Lylo flags it for review instead of hiding the assumption. The solicitor can check it, change it, or decide what should be used.

00:00:46.000 --> 00:00:58.000
You can edit the draft yourself, just like a normal document. Or, tell Lylo what you want changed in chat, and Lylo can update it for you.

00:00:58.000 --> 00:01:05.500
You can also add more heads of loss, such as notice pay, holiday pay, benefits, interest and more.

00:01:05.500 --> 00:01:15.500
The result is a clear, reviewable Schedule of Loss, with the evidence, calculations and assumptions all visible in one place.
